      </p>
      <p>
        You represent that you own or have the necessary rights to the
        content you submit, and that it doesn't infringe anyone else's
        intellectual property rights or violate any law or right of
        privacy.
      </p>

      <h2>5. AI features</h2>
      <p>
        The Service may include AI-powered features (for example, shot
        recommendations and post-round summaries via the "AI Caddie"
        feature when enabled). <strong>The AI Caddie is currently
        disabled in this build of the app.</strong> This section applies
        whenever the feature is re-enabled.
      </p>
      <p>
        AI output is generated probabilistically and may be inaccurate or
        inappropriate for your situation. Use your own judgment — the AI
        Caddie is for entertainment and should not be relied on as
        professional coaching. We do not guarantee that AI output will
        improve your scoring.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Side games and tournaments — money between players</h2>
      <p>
        Bagpipe Golf includes side-game and tournament scoring features
        that track money flow between players. <strong>Money wagered
        between players never passes through Bagpipe Golf.</strong>
        Players settle those wagers between themselves, outside the app.
        We compute who-owes-whom and display the result; for
        player-to-player wagers we do not hold, transfer, or escrow the
        stakes and we do not act as a payment processor.
      </p>
      <p>
        You are solely responsible for ensuring that your bets and
        tournaments are lawful in your jurisdiction and that you handle
        the resulting payments lawfully (including any tax obligations).
        If you choose to invite others to bet, you represent that all
        participants are eligible to participate in those bets where
        they live.
      </p>
      <p>
        Money we <em>do</em> handle is a separate thing from the wagers
        above: subscription plans, single-event passes, and — where a
        director has it switched on — card entry fees. All of that is
        covered in §7.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Plans, payments and subscriptions</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Taybuta, Inc.</strong>, doing business as Bagpipe Golf,
        is the seller for everything described in this section. Payments
        are taken by <strong>Stripe</strong>, our payment processor, on a
        Stripe-hosted checkout page. <strong>We never receive or store
        your full card number, expiry, or security code.</strong> Prices
        are in U.S. dollars and are the prices in force on the "Last
        updated" date above.
      </p>

      <h3>What we sell</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>An event pass</strong> — a one-time charge covering a single tournament. Smaller fields are free; the player count at which a pass is required is published with the price.</li>
        <li><strong>A League plan</strong> — an annual subscription covering one league, one organizer login, and unlimited events in that league.</li>
        <li><strong>A Club plan</strong> — an annual subscription covering unlimited leagues and multiple admin accounts. Club plans are currently set up with us directly rather than fully self-serve.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>Current prices, and what each plan includes, are published
        on our <a href="/pricing">pricing page</a> and shown again at
        checkout before you pay.</strong> Prices are subject to change, and
        the price that applies to you is the one shown when you buy — see
        "Price changes and taxes" below.
      </p>
      <p>
        Players are never charged by us to take part in a league or
        tournament someone else has paid for. A league or tournament host
        may separately collect dues or an entry fee from their players;
        that is their charge, not ours, and it is covered below.
      </p>

      <h3>Free trial</h3>
      <p>
        A league organizer may start <strong>one</strong> free trial of
        <strong>30 days</strong>, with no card required. The trial is one
        per organizer, not one per league. Club trials are arranged with
        us directly. If a trial ends without a paid plan, the league
        locks as described below — nothing is charged and nothing is
        deleted.
      </p>

      <h3>Automatic renewal and cancellation</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>League and Club plans renew automatically each year</strong>
        until you cancel. At each renewal we charge your saved payment
        method the then-current price for another year. Single-event
        passes do not renew.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can cancel at any time from the billing page in your account.
        <strong>Cancelling takes effect at the end of the period you have
        already paid for</strong>, and you keep full access until then; we
        do not cut access off mid-term.
      </p>

      <h3>Promotional codes</h3>
      <p>
        We sometimes offer promotional or launch codes. Where we do, the
        terms of that particular code — what it discounts, which plans
        it covers, and how long it can be redeemed — are stated
        wherever we publish it, and it is valid only on the terms stated
        there. Unless we say otherwise in writing, a code applies to the
        <strong>first payment only</strong>: renewals are charged at the
        full then-current price. One code per checkout.
      </p>

      <h3>Refunds of what you buy from us</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>What this covers:</strong> the Single Event pass, the
        League plan, and the Club plan — the things you buy from Bagpipe
        Golf.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>You have 7 days.</strong> Ask us within <strong>7 days of
        the purchase</strong>, at the address in §16, and we will refund
        it. After 7 days those payments are non-refundable except where
        the law requires otherwise.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you think you have been charged in error, or something went
        wrong with a charge, contact us whether or not the 7 days have
        passed.
      </p>

      <h3>Refunds of player dues — the director's call, not ours</h3>
      <p>
        Dues and entry fees a player pays a league or tournament are
        <strong>not our money and not our decision</strong>.
        <strong>Whether a player is refunded, when, and on what terms is
        entirely at the discretion of the league director or tournament
        host.</strong> They set their own policy and issue any refund from
        their own tools.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>The 7-day window above does not apply to player dues.</strong>
        We do not impose a deadline, a condition, or a right to a refund on
        that relationship, and we do not arbitrate it — a question or
        dispute about dues or an entry fee is between the player and their
        director.
      </p>
      <p>
        One mechanical point, so a director can price their own policy:
        when a dues refund is issued the player gets their <strong>full
        payment back</strong> on their card, while <strong>our 2% platform
        fee is not returned</strong>, and neither is the card processor's
        own fee. Both are borne by the league or tournament, not deducted
        from the player.
      </p>

      <h3>Failed payments, and what happens if a plan lapses</h3>
      <p>
        If a renewal payment fails, Stripe retries it for a short period
        and your plan stays active while it does. If the payment
        ultimately cannot be collected, the plan lapses.
      </p>
      <p>
        While a league has no active plan, the organizer can no longer
        start a new season, add events, or attach tournaments to it.
        <strong>Your existing leagues, events, rounds, and scores remain,
        and nothing is deleted because of non-payment.</strong> Players
        keep access to what has already been played. Subscribing again
        restores the controls.
      </p>

      <h3>Price changes and taxes</h3>
      <p>
